{title: 136 - Good Christians, Now Rejoice}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #136 • IN DULCE JUBILO • 6.6.7.7.7.8.5.5}
{lyricist: John M. Neale}
{composer: 14th century melody}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 136}
{meta: tune IN DULCE JUBILO}
{meta: meter 6.6.7.7.7.8.5.5}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Good Christians, [Am]now [C/G]rejoice,
[Am/C]With heart, and soul, and [C/G]voice;
[C/G]Give [C7/Bb]ye heed to what [Dm/A]we [Am]say:
[F/C]Jesus Christ is born [C7]today;
[C7/Bb]Ox and [Dm/A]ass [C]before Him [Gm/D]bow,
[F/C]And He is in the manger [Am]now.
[C/G]Christ [F]is born [Gm/D]today!
[Bb]Christ is born today!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]Good Christians, [Am]now [C/G]rejoice,
[Am/C]With heart, and soul, and [C/G]voice;
[C/G]Now [C7/Bb]ye hear of endless [Am]bliss:
[F/C]Jesus Christ was born [C7]for this!
[C7/Bb]He hath [Dm/A]ope'd [C]the heav'nly [Gm/D]door,
[F/C]And we are blessed evermore.
[C/G]Christ [F]was born [Gm/D]for [Am]this!
[Bb]Christ was born for this!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]Good Christians, [Am]now [C/G]rejoice,
[Am/C]With heart, and soul, and [C/G]voice;
[C/G]Now [C7/Bb]ye need not fear [Dm/A]the [Am]grave:
[F/C]Jesus Christ was born [C7]to save!
[C7/Bb]Calls you [Dm/A]one [C]and calls you [Gm/D]all
[F/C]To gain His everlasting [Am]hall.
[C/G]Christ [F]was born [Gm/D]to [Am]save!
[Bb]Christ was born to save!
{end_of_verse}
